additionalEmails.description:
Add additional email addresses to a contact.

> ⚠️ **Important:** When sending `additionalEmails`, you must also include the contact’s current primary `email` in the same request.<br>If you send `additionalEmails` without `email`, the contact’s existing primary email may be cleared or replaced.

<ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem">
<li style="list-style: disc"><code>email</code> represents the contact’s <strong>primary email address</strong>.</li>
<li style="list-style: disc"><code>additionalEmails</code> represents secondary email addresses for the same contact.</li>
<li style="list-style: disc">Always send the primary <code>email</code> together with <code>additionalEmails</code> when updating email addresses.</li>
<li style="list-style: disc">A maximum of <strong>10 additional email addresses</strong> can be provided.</li>
</ul>

Example

```json
{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "additionalEmails": [
    {
      "email": "john.work@example.com"
    }
  ]
}
```

Avoid

```json
{
  "additionalEmails": [
    {
      "email": "john.work@example.com"
    }
  ]
}
```

Sending only `additionalEmails` may cause the existing primary email to be lost.

If email uniqueness is enabled for the location, every email address in the request—primary and additional—must be unique across contacts. If any email already belongs to another contact, the request fails with **400 Bad Request** and no changes are saved.

